ive are illustrative; the grade and the line of the track are real.","Trees, shrubs, grass tufts and boulders are placed where WorldCover maps that cover; their size and number are illustrative.","The walking loop is a 150 m circle around the arrival point; it is not a mapped trail.","Trees within 25 m of the Jahanabad Buddha are left out so it can be seen; WorldCover 2021 maps tree cover there.","The boulder is the Atlas's procedural model: a rounded granite mass about 12 x 11 x 9 m, flattened on the carved face and sunk 1 m into the slope; its size, lumps and weathering tones are estimated (no survey).","The Buddha in relief is drawn to the published size: the carved figure is 7 m high and 5 m wide (700 x 500 cm), its throne 1.2 m high and 3.9 m wide (120 x 390 cm); the relief stands 0.11 m proud of the niche floor. The oval niche (about 8.8 x 8.4 m) and its depth of 0.3 m are estimated. The folds, hands, head and halo are estimated from the published description and the photos.","The figure's foot is set 1 m above the ground at the face (estimated).","Trees within 25 m of the carving are left out so it can be seen; WorldCover maps tree cover there. A timber viewing deck (about 3.6 x 1.5 m) and a few boulders in front are estimated from the photos.","No steps are mapped in OSM and none show in the photos, so none are drawn; the walk up from the road is traced over the ground (easiest slope on the DEM).","The carving is drawn restored and without the 2007 damage to the head.","The walk from the end of the jeep track follows the mapped OSM footpath for 0.0 km; the last 0.69 km is not mapped and is traced over the ground (easiest slope on the DEM).","Season colours, snow, ice and dawn mist are illustrative.","Traffic on the drive is illustrative: the vehicle kinds are those seen on Swat roads (Willys jeeps, Hilux, Suzuki vans, Mehran cars, CD70 motorbikes, Qingqi rickshaws, painted trucks); their number and movement are not counted."],"sources":[{"name":"Copernicus DEM GLO-30","use":"terrain heights","licence":"© DLR e.V. 2010-2014 and © Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014-2018, provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA","url":"https://spacedata.copernicus.eu/collections/copernicus-digital-elevation-model"},{"name":"ESA WorldCover 10 m 2021 v200","use":"trees, meadow, rock, snow","licence":"CC BY 4.0, © ESA WorldCover project 2021","url":"https://esa-worldcover.org"},{"name":"Buddhist rock carving in Manglawar (Wikipedia)","use":"size of the Jahan-Abad-i relief (700 x 500 cm, asana 120 x 390 cm), its orientation (facing north west), its 2007 damage and restoration","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0 (Wikipedia text)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buddhist_rock_carving_in_Manglawar"},{"name":"OpenStreetMap","use":"the Malam Jabba Road (S-15) to the point where the mapped departure to the Buddha begins, and the Buddha node","licence":"ODbL, © OpenStreetMap contributors","url":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright"}]}